  "description": "SEZGEN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C58 H66 Gd4 N18 O20. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.882-3.945 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.60-110.86°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C58H66Gd4N18O20. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
